# Feature folders

This is a static prototype. Screens are **surface → epic → screen**, not a flat `js/` dump.

- Markup belongs in `features/<surface>/<epic>/<screen>/<screen>.html`
- Unique CSS/JS live in that same folder
- Shared epic chrome goes in that epic's `shared/`
- Demo chrome is `features/shell/`
- Do not rebuild screens as JavaScript template strings
- Do not edit `css/app.css`, `js/bundle.js`, or `js/generated/templates.js`
- After HTML/CSS/JS changes run `npm run build`
- Read the nearest `AGENTS.md` before editing
